ocm\",\"device-visibility\",\"enablement\",\"magpie\"]},{\"what\":\"The bench-client domino from the prior round is CLEARED: /opt/venv/bin/python3 imports huggingface_hub 1.29.0 + transformers 5.16.1 successfully, so the recorded setup_commands have been replayed and no further install is needed.\",\"source\":\"in-session: /opt/venv/bin/python3 -c 'import huggingface_hub, transformers'\",\"expected_impact\":\"Removes the last known post-boot blocker for producing inferencex_result.json.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none\",\"domain_tags\":[\"environment\",\"magpie\",\"inferencex\"]},{\"what\":\"attempt[1] (15:14) reached server bind and died on 'OSError: [Errno 98] Address already in use' on port 8888, i.e. a stale server survived the prior failed attempt; port 8888 is free NOW. Mechanism is real: an APIServer that dies leaves VLLM::EngineCore orphaned (observed in-session: pid 12279 held ~3.7GB after its parent exited).\",\"source\":\"runs/baseline/48e0ae2b.../server.log; in-session orphan observation\",\"expected_impact\":\"Explains a launch failure that looks model-side but is port lifecycle; must not be fixed by killing foreign pids.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"none\",\"domain_tags\":[\"magpie\",\"vllm\",\"lifecycle\",\"enablement\"]}],\"patches_written\":[],\"proposal_set\":[{\"name\":\"mask_reconcile_logical_hip\",\"args_mode\":\"append\",\"atomic\":true,\"extra_args\":\"\",\"extra_envs\":{\"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\":\"0\",\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\":\"0\"},\"remove_args\":[],\"unset_envs\":[],\"reason\":\"Production leaks HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 (physical) while the yaml pins ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0; ROCR re-indexes so HIP must carry the LOGICAL 0. Reproduced: leaked -> EngineCore 'No CUDA GPUs are available'; HIP=0 -> full boot + health 200 + correct tokens. Mirrors Magpie's own gpu_selection rule (benchmarker.py:519-522).\",\"kb_evidence\":[],\"pr_evidence\":[],\"source_evidence\":[\"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:519-522\",\"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156\"]}],\"residual_questions\":[\"Was attempt[1] on port 8888 a stale-server artifact of attempt[0]? If the coordinator sees Errno 98 again, a pre-flight port release (not a foreign kill) is the fix.\"],\"summary\":\"Diagnosis-only so far: model IS runnable (proven boot + inference on GPU0); current blocker is the leaked HIP mask (reproduced) plus a transient port-8888 conflict. Authoring the smallest bridge.\"}}\nEOF\nmv $D/specialist_done.partial.json.tmp $D/specialist_done.partial.json; python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$D/specialist_done.partial.json'));print('partial OK')\"; date -u +%s","description":"Checkpoint partial result with findings"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07dcb743-e9fb-4243-9b9b-dfe12b493268","uuid":"6180f8c0-0a18-4209-a05f-a9806aa8c6ea"}
