 capital of Germany is Berlin.'; chat 17+25 -> '42').\",\n        \"source\": \"/mnt/stripe-3mix-3t2/models/davetha/Qwen3.8-27B-ABLITERATED-W8A8-gdnint8/config.json; /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py:203-204,592-595; in-session logs/repro_server.log + logs/reproB_fixed.log (port 8899, GPU 0, exact production server_args from manifest.json)\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Reframes the whole round: no ladder climb (Rung 2-5) is needed for this model; the entire blocker is launch-environment hygiene, so a config-only delta suffices.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"qwen3_5\", \"gdn\", \"hybrid_attention\", \"runnability\", \"enablement\", \"gfx90a\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"CONFIRMED BY A/B ON THE PRODUCTION GATE PATH, with the kept Magpie patch NOT live (it applies cleanly but is currently reverted in the tree): the harness inherits ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 + HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2. Equal counts, so torch._parse_visible_devices() passes and vLLM binds the socket, then EngineCore dies at worker init_device -> torch._C._cuda_init() -> 'RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available'. ROCR re-indexes the surviving agent to logical 0, so a physical id 2 in HIP selects nothing. Control run (same leaked env, no delta) = that exact traceback; candidate run (only extra_envs HIP/CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0) = status SUCCESS, /health 200, inferencex_result.json, output_throughput 110.19 tok/s, TTFT 1437 ms, TPOT 34.9 ms.\",\n        \"source\": \"in-session scratch/e2e_control/.../server.log (RuntimeError at gpu_worker.py:379 -> torch/cuda/__init__.py:501) vs scratch/e2e_fixed/.../inferencex_result.json + logs/e2e_fixed.json; /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch/cuda/__init__.py; vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156 (_sync_hip_cuda_env_vars)\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"This is the single blocker for booting at all; pinning HIP/CUDA to the logical index clears it (proven, not inferred).\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"rocm\", \"device-visibility\", \"enablement\", \"magpie\", \"inferencex\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"Only TWO config mechanisms exist to fix the leak, and they are NOT equivalent. (a) A variant's extra_envs lands in benchmark.envs, which Magpie writes OVER an os.environ.copy() in _build_local_command (benchmarker.py:776 'env = os.environ.copy()', then :800 'for key, value in env_vars.items(): env[key] = str(value)') -> it DOES override an inherited leak. (b) unset_envs only pops the key from the YAML dict (_grid_runner.py:664-669), and Magpie re-adds the inherited value from os.environ -> it CANNOT remove an inherited var. Also, removing HIP entirely would NOT work: the InferenceX launcher derives HIP from ROCR only under '[ -z \\\"$HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\\\" ]' (vllm_mi300x.sh:65-68), which an inherited value defeats. So an explicit extra_envs pin is the only patch-free fix, and HIP must be set to a VALUE, not unset.\",\n        \"source\": \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:776,800; /opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/hyperloom/orchestrator/actions/executors/_grid_runner.py:664-671; InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:63-68\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Prevents a future round from proposing unset_envs / 'just unset HIP', which look right but are inert against an inherited var.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"hyperloom\", \"magpie\", \"grid_semantics\", \"enablement\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"HIP and CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES must be set TOGETHER and EQUAL. vLLM's _sync_hip_cuda_env_vars() raises a hard ValueError on a HIP/CUDA disagreement, and copies an inherited CUDA value onto HIP when HIP is unset. So a one-sided pin (HIP=0 with a leaked CUDA=<physical>) converts a device-selection bug into an import-time crash. The proposed variant is therefore marked atomic=true with both vars pinned to 0. Empirically validated: the successful run had ROCR=0 + HIP=0 + CUDA=0 all set (vLLM emits only the 'CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES on ROCm is deprecated' warning).\",\n        \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156; in-session scratch/e2e_fixed/.../config.yaml lines 18,26-27 + server.log (boot succeeded with all three set)\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Makes the enablement delta robust to whichever mask the harness happens to leak, instead of trading one failure for another.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"vllm\", \"rocm\", \"device-visibility\", \"enablement\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"The prior round's next-domino blockers are BOTH already resolved, so nothing further is needed from them. (1) bench-client deps: /opt/venv/bin/python3 (first on the gate's PATH, used by benchmark_lib.sh's bare 'python3') now imports huggingface_hub 1.29.0 + transformers 5.16.1, i.e. the recorded setup_commands were replayed and the ModuleNotFoundError that killed the earlier client is gone. (2) lm-eval is self-installing at eval time (benchmark_lib.sh:870-885 _install_lm_eval_deps, pip '|| true'), so it needs no pre-provisioning. (3) attempt[1]'s 'OSError: [Errno 98] Address already in use' on port 8888 was a stale-server artifact of attempt[0], not a model gap: nothing listens on 88xx/89xx now and GPU 0 VRAM is back to ~11 MB, and the mechanism is real (an APIServer that dies leaves VLLM::EngineCore orphaned - observed in-session as pid 12279 holding memory after its parent exited).\",\n        \"source\": \"in-session /opt/venv/bin/python3 -c 'import huggingface_hub, transformers'; InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/benchmark_lib.sh:682,870-885; runs/baseline/48e0ae2b.../server.log; ps/ss/rocm-smi probes\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Removes two phantom gaps from the stack so the next round can spend its budget on the real gate (accuracy/throughput) instead of re-diagnosing the launcher.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"environment\", \"magpie\", \"inferencex\", \"lifecycle\", \"enablement\"]\n      },\n      {\n        \"what\": \"CRITICAL ROUTING FACT for patch authoring in this session: the serving interpreter is NOT the allowlisted /opt/envs/vllm tree. VLLM_BIN=/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w execs /opt/envs/wu1w/bin/python -m vllm.entrypoints.cli.main, so enablement patches authored against /opt/envs/vllm/.../vllm are INERT. The two trees are near-identical 0.28.0 builds differing in exactly 3 source files, and /opt/envs/wu1w carries prior optimization work (an is_aiter_attention_supported() gfx90a carve-out that widens AITER Linear past the stock CDNA3-only gate, plus a fused_gdn_hip op fallback and relaxed num_v_heads==8*num_k_heads -> divisibility for GDN MTP). Magpie itself is only in /opt/envs/vllm, which is why the kept patch targets Magpie and is valid.\",\n        \"source\": \"/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w; diff -rq --exclude=__pycache__ of the two vllm trees (3 files: _aiter_ops.py, _custom_ops.py, model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py); state.json enablement.framework_root; manifest.json dependencies.magpie.path\",\n        \"expected_impact\": \"Explains how a prior round's patch could be approved, integrated and still change nothing; redirects all future vllm-side authoring to the live tree or to a proposal instead.\",\n        \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\",\n        \"domain_tags\": [\"integration\", \"allowlist\", \"venv-routing\", \"enablement\", \"aiter\", \"gdn\"]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"proposal_set\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"rocm_logical_hip_mask_pin\",\n        \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n        \"atomic\": true,\n        \"extra_args\": \"\",\n        \"extra_envs\": {\n          \"HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES\": \"0\",\n          \"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\": \"0\"\n        },\n        \"remove_args\": [],\n        \"unset_envs\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Makes the combo boot. The harness inherits HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 (a PHYSICAL id) while the gate config pins ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0; ROCR filters at the HSA layer and re-indexes survivors to 0..n-1, so HIP must carry the LOGICAL index. Counts are equal, so torch's length check passes and the failure lands deeper and illegibly: EngineCore 'RuntimeError: No CUDA GPUs are available' at init_device. PROVEN on the real Magpie/InferenceX path under the identical inherited leak, with the kept patch NOT applied: control (no delta) reproduces the crash; this delta alone yields status SUCCESS, /health 200, inferencex_result.json and 110.19 tok/s output. extra_envs (not unset_envs) is required - unset only pops the YAML dict while Magpie re-adds the inherited value from os.environ, and the launcher's '[ -z HIP ]' derivation cannot fire on an inherited value. Both vars are set equal and together because vLLM raises ValueError on any HIP/CUDA disagreement and copies an inherited CUDA onto HIP. Scoped TP=1 (this session's fixed TP), where the logical set is exactly {0}; mirrors Magpie's own gpu_selection rule at benchmarker.py:519-522.\",\n        \"kb_evidence\": [\n          \"framework: ROCR re-indexes to 0..n-1 so HIP takes logical indices (Magpie's own documented rule, benchmarker.py:517-522)\",\n          \"in-session A/B: leaked HIP=2 -> EngineCore 'No CUDA GPUs are available'; HIP=0 -> full boot, 35/35 graphs, /health 200, correct tokens, 110.19 tok/s\"\n        ],\n        \"pr_evidence\": [],\n        \"source_evidence\": [\n          \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:776,800 (config envs override os.environ copy)\",\n          \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/Magpie/modes/benchmark/benchmarker.py:517-522 (HIP must be logical 0..N-1 after ROCR filtering)\",\n          \"/opt/envs/vllm/lib/python3.12/site-packages/hyperloom/orchestrator/actions/executors/_grid_runner.py:664-671 (unset_envs pops only from the YAML dict)\",\n          \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:127-156 (_sync_hip_cuda_env_vars raises on HIP/CUDA disagreement)\",\n          \"InferenceX@3d55815/benchmarks/vllm_mi300x.sh:63-68 (derivation guarded by -z HIP, so it cannot repair an inherited value)\",\n          \"scratch/e2e_fixed/variant_00_specialist-rebench/benchmark_vllm_20260914_153258/inferencex_result.json\",\n          \"scratch/e2e_control/variant_00_specialist-rebench/benchmark_vllm_20260914_153851/server.log\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"patches_written\": [],\n    \"artifacts_written\": [],\n    \"setup_commands\": [],\n    \"residual_questions\": [\n      \"EVAL-PATH RISK the coordinator should watch at the accuracy gate (I did NOT touch it - changing it would be altering the eval contract): this checkpoint's chat_template.jinja injects a large built-in operator system prompt plus xhigh reasoning-effort instructions. Measured live: a 12-token one-line user question cost prompt_tokens=1225. The model also emits a long <|im_start|> reasoning block before its answer (seen in the chat probe: it reasoned out loud then printed '42'). If the gate's gsm8k eval goes through /v1/chat/completions, that ~1.2k-token prefix and the CoT tail can push against max_model_len=6144 and can defeat strict/regex answer extraction; if it goes through /v1/completions with the yaml's own utils/evals/gsm8k.yaml few-shot, it likely does not. Worth confirming which endpoint run_lm_eval uses before reading a low accuracy as a quantization regression.\",\n      \"Should the next round keep BOTH the approved Magpie reconciliation patch and this env pin? They are mutually consistent (both resolve to HIP=0), so either alone is sufficient and both together are harmless - but if integrate_patch's re-application of 001_reconcile_rocm_device_masks.patch ever fails, this proposal is the patch-free safety net that still boots. I did not author a replacement patch to avoid a redundant duplicate of already-approved work.\",\n      \"Port hygiene: attempt[1] died on 'OSError: [Errno 98] Address already in use' on the gate port 8888 because a server from the failed attempt[0] still held it. Is there a pre-flight port release between baseline attempts? I deliberately did NOT kill any foreign pid (Iron Rule 7), so this can recur on a retry-after-failure and would again be misclassified as a model-side launch failure.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\nJSONEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('$D/scratch/final.json'))\np=d['payload']\nprint('JSON valid. empty=',p['empty'],'conf=',p['confidence'])\nprint('proposals=',len(p['proposal_set']),'findings=',len(p['new_findings']),'patches=',p['patches_written'])\nprint('summary len=',len(p['summary']))\nassert len(p['summary'])<=500, 'summary too long'\nprint('names:',[x['name'] for x in p['proposal_set']])\nprint('OK')\n\"","description":"Author final payload and validate"}}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07dcb743-e9fb-4243-9b9b-dfe12b493268","uuid":"59de1a1f-94fb-4b1e-b436-362833f19bc3"}
